// @expect-compile-fail unresolvable identifier is also a hard error
// An identifier the type checker cannot resolve is reported with its real
// source line. It used to say "…hml:0:" because the parser never stamped
// line/column onto identifier expressions. Resolving to nothing is also a
// hard error, so the compile failure below is expected and part of the
// asserted output -- the point of the fixture is the ":3:" in the warning.
let a = 1;
let b = 2;
print("" + NOPE);
